# Optional patterns: review each against the receiving project.
# Preserve intentional AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, skills, docs, tests, workflows,
# lockfiles, LICENSE/NOTICE files, and required attribution.
# Do not ignore an entire tool configuration directory without inspecting it.

# Local sessions and scratch work: use only directories your project reserves.
/.local-agent-sessions/
/.local-agent-cache/
/.local-agent-logs/
/.local-prompt-drafts/
/.local-chat-transcripts/
/.local-scratch/

# Development prompt/recording dumps, when these exact files are local inputs.
# Keep product runtime prompts and intentional toolkit source versioned.
/PROMPT.md
/DEMO_SCRIPT.md
/uiux.md
/uiux.txt

# Dedicated local media-production workspaces, when separate from app source.
/video/
/videos/
/creative-production-toolkit/

# Local credentials/configuration; allow reviewed examples.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime and build products: adapt to the actual stack.
/dist/
/build/
/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
*.tmp
*.tsbuildinfo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Ignore rules do not remove already tracked files or revoke leaked secrets.
# Check for intentionally versioned .pem/.key fixtures and exempt them if needed.
